{"name":"Chimney Sweep","hex":"#272f38","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"chimney sweep","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person whose job is to clean soot from chimneys."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chimney_sweep"}],"entries":[{"title":"Chimney sweep","blocks":[{"text":"A chimney sweep is a person who inspects then clears soot and creosote from chimneys. The chimney uses the pressure difference caused by a hot column of gas to create a draught and draw air over the hot coals or wood enabling continued combustion. Chimneys may be straight or contain many changes of direction. During normal operation, a layer of creosote builds up on the inside of the chimney, restricting the flow. The creosote can also catch fire, setting the chimney alight. The chimney must be swept to remove the soot."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Chimneysweep.png/330px-Chimneysweep.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chimney_sweep","wikidata":"Q506126"},{"title":"Chimney","blocks":[{"text":"A chimney is an architectural ventilation structure made of masonry, clay or metal that isolates hot toxic exhaust gases or smoke produced by a boiler, stove, furnace, incinerator, or fireplace from human living areas. Chimneys are typically vertical, or as near as possible to vertical, to ensure that the gases flow smoothly, drawing air into the combustion in what is known as the stack, or chimney effect. The space inside a chimney is called the flue. Chimneys are adjacent to large industrial refineries, fossil fuel combustion facilities or part of buildings, steam locomotives and ships."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chimney","wikidata":"Q170477"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/Women_at_work_during_the_First_World_War_Q30759.jpg/500px-Women_at_work_during_the_First_World_War_Q30759.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/Women_at_work_during_the_First_World_War_Q30759.jpg/1280px-Women_at_work_during_the_First_World_War_Q30759.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/Women_at_work_during_the_First_World_War_Q30759.jpg/500px-Women_at_work_during_the_First_World_War_Q30759.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A chimney sweep in Kent, England, 1918","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWomen_at_work_during_the_First_World_War_Q30759.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Bub_und_Meister.JPG/500px-Bub_und_Meister.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Bub_und_Meister.JPG/1280px-Bub_und_Meister.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Bub_und_Meister.JPG/500px-Bub_und_Meister.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A master chimney sweep (right) and his apprentice boy, known as a Spazzacamino, in Italy at the end of the 19th century","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABub_und_Meister.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Sotare_p%C3%A5_ett_tak_i_Stockholm.jpg/500px-Sotare_p%C3%A5_ett_tak_i_Stockholm.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Sotare_p%C3%A5_ett_tak_i_Stockholm.jpg/1280px-Sotare_p%C3%A5_ett_tak_i_Stockholm.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Sotare_p%C3%A5_ett_tak_i_Stockholm.jpg/500px-Sotare_p%C3%A5_ett_tak_i_Stockholm.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Chimney sweepers on a roof in Stockholm in the early 20th century","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASotare_p%C3%A5_ett_tak_i_Stockholm.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Seven-flue_Stack_1834.png/330px-Seven-flue_Stack_1834.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Seven-flue_Stack_1834.png/330px-Seven-flue_Stack_1834.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cross-section of a seven-flue stack in a four-story house with cellars. An 1834 illustration from Mechanics' Magazine, designed to show the contrast between mechanical sweeping and children sweeping chimneys.A. a hearth served by vertical flue, a horizontal flue, and then a vertical rise having two right-angled bends that were difficult for brushes.B. a long straight flue (14in by 9in) being climbed by a boy using back, elbows, and knees.C. a short flue from a second floor hearth. The climbing boy has reached the chimney pot, which has a diameter too small for him to exit that way.E. shows a disaster. The climbing boy is stuck in the flue, his knees jammed against his chin.G. How a flue could be straightened to make it sweepable by mechanical meansH. A dead climbing boy, suffocated in a fall of soot that accumulated at the cant of the flue.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASeven-flue_Stack_1834.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Frederick_Daniel_Hardy_%281827-1911%29_-_The_Chimney_Sweep_-_OP343_-_Bantock_House_Museum.jpg/500px-Frederick_Daniel_Hardy_%281827-1911%29_-_The_Chimney_Sweep_-_OP343_-_Bantock_House_Museum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Frederick_Daniel_Hardy_%281827-1911%29_-_The_Chimney_Sweep_-_OP343_-_Bantock_House_Museum.jpg/500px-Frederick_Daniel_Hardy_%281827-1911%29_-_The_Chimney_Sweep_-_OP343_-_Bantock_House_Museum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Chimney Sweep by Frederick Daniel Hardy, 1866","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFrederick_Daniel_Hardy_(1827-1911)_-_The_Chimney_Sweep_-_OP343_-_Bantock_House_Museum.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Studio_portrait_of_young_chimney_sweeps%2C_by_Havens%2C_O._Pierre_1838-1912_%28crop%29.jpg/250px-Studio_portrait_of_young_chimney_sweeps%2C_by_Havens%2C_O._Pierre_1838-1912_%28crop%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a3/Studio_portrait_of_young_chimney_sweeps%2C_by_Havens%2C_O._Pierre_1838-1912_%28crop%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Studio_portrait_of_young_chimney_sweeps%2C_by_Havens%2C_O._Pierre_1838-1912_%28crop%29.jpg/250px-Studio_portrait_of_young_chimney_sweeps%2C_by_Havens%2C_O._Pierre_1838-1912_%28crop%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A studio portrait of four New York climbing boys, with brushes and scrapers","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStudio_portrait_of_young_chimney_sweeps%2C_by_Havens%2C_O._Pierre_1838-1912_(crop).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Chimney_sweep_modern.jpg/330px-Chimney_sweep_modern.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Chimney_sweep_modern.jpg/330px-Chimney_sweep_modern.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Modern chimney sweep","link":"https://en.wikip